{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/c8afd229cbf92cbaea64dbc442a493c4.avif?t=1757698469\" width=596 height=110 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>The location?</strong> Tokyo. <strong>The year?</strong> It\u2019s - hey, let\u2019s come back to that. <strong>What\u2019s happening?</strong>\u00a0Well... it\u2019s your job to find out.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In <i>Mysteries of Old Tokyo,</i> you\u2019re the new researcher and investigator for the Tokyo branch of the secretive Rare Items Acquisitions Ltd. You\u2019ll walk the streets of the Imperial Capital and use your database of facts to interrogate a host of wandering spirits, find out their histories, lies, and truths, and unlock over 40 real-life locations. Travelling through space and time, a database of hundreds of Tokyo hotspots, transit networks and people creates new stories every time you play.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/b57d2749f936e6f95e21fa4773c67232.poster.avif?t=1757698469\" width=480 height=320 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/b57d2749f936e6f95e21fa4773c67232.webm?t=1757698469\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/b57d2749f936e6f95e21fa4773c67232.mp4?t=1757698469\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Inspired by the CD-ROM &quot;multimedia experiences&quot; of the 1990s like <i>Encarta '96</i> and <i>Cosmology of Kyoto</i>, as well as modern detective games like\u00a0<i>The Roottrees are Dead</i> and the <i>Golden Idol</i>\u00a0series,\u00a0<i><strong>Mysteries of Old Tokyo</strong></i>\u00a0takes a set of postcards printed in 1930s Tokyo from the author's collection and brings them, hand-scanned, to your personal computer in <strong>full 1024x768 resolution</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/29ca5075d57098565d53eebe0a1e01c3.avif?t=1757698469\" width=596 height=110 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Start your morning at the office, using real-life facts and photographs to sort and categorise incoming data. </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Who was Dai Nank\u014d? Who built the Eitai Bridge? What became of the Rokumeikan?</i> It\u2019s your research skills that will uncover the fascinating stories behind over 40 postcards, covering hundreds of years of Tokyo\u2019s history, both good and bad.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/e6a5caab5933f711b0dbc1902edaf5ee.poster.avif?t=1757698469\" width=640 height=480 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/e6a5caab5933f711b0dbc1902edaf5ee.webm?t=1757698469\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/e6a5caab5933f711b0dbc1902edaf5ee.mp4?t=1757698469\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/f9398c74256243cdc7df0300bf2df1fc.avif?t=1757698469\" width=596 height=110 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >After lunch, step out- or take a train - into the streets of Tokyo, past and present. </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Track down the wandering spirits</strong> plaguing the city, from flirty courtesan Kasuga-dono to the tragic Lieutenant Ando, and <strong>separate the truth from their lies</strong>.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Use the databases at your disposal to <strong>identify the inconsistencies</strong> in their stories. </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>How could they have been on that bridge when it was demolished in 1956? Was it really possible to get from Ueno to Tokyo in 23 minutes before the Yamanote Line was built?</i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >When you think you know what really happened, present your case to the spirit and boost your social link. </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Help them find their truth one chapter at a time, inspired by the real histories of the people of Tokyo<i>.</i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Visit postcards depicting over <strong>40 Tokyo landmarks</strong>, from present-day tourist hotspots to long-forgotten obscurities, including:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Asakusa Senso-ji Temple</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Meiji Shrine</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Shinjuku</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ginza</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ueno Park</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/a26538d75f273fcaaf073ddb330a653a.avif?t=1757698469\" width=596 height=110 /></span></h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Explore a <strong>detailed database of Tokyo\u2019s extensive train network</strong>, from <strong>Akabane</strong> to <strong>Zoshigaya</strong>, covering over 150 years. </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This database used to generate unique stories for the spirits, but you can explore it yourself to get <strong>turn-by-turn public transport directions</strong> in Tokyo for any year between 1872 (the first railway in Tokyo) to 2025 - <strong>just in case you ever find yourself going back in time.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/1bd38aabd51c51c30f44212539d66b73.poster.avif?t=1757698469\" width=640 height=480 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/1bd38aabd51c51c30f44212539d66b73.webm?t=1757698469\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/1bd38aabd51c51c30f44212539d66b73.mp4?t=1757698469\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As an agent for Rare Item Acquisitions, you'll come to know Tokyo like the back of your hand. As you explore, plot the best routes using Tokyo\u2019s historical train networks to save time <i>and </i>money. <strong>Your expense account is <i>not</i> bottomless</strong>!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As well as over 40 postcards you can visit, the game database includes hundreds of historical Tokyo hotspots and train stations that are used to <strong>generate unique stories every time you play</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/c820d7880e050ab8c2e64affba6fd1f4.avif?t=1757698469\" width=596 height=110 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >As you play, you\u2019ll <strong>unlock new postcards, uncover the personal backstories of each wandering spirit</strong>, and <strong>acquire fabulous treasures for your employer</strong>.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Brand new photography</strong> from 2025, aligned and matched with the original postcards, lets you see these postcards in a modern context. Plus, learn all about each location with the original 1930s postcard description (<strong>translated for the first time from Japanese</strong>) complemented by present-day updates covering the last 90 years of Japanese history and more.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/06dbafe0622a88ff0aed694bb2dd87db.poster.avif?t=1757698469\" width=480 height=360 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/06dbafe0622a88ff0aed694bb2dd87db.webm?t=1757698469\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/06dbafe0622a88ff0aed694bb2dd87db.mp4?t=1757698469\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Whenever you find a new treasure, you can head over to the 3D viewer to examine it in <strong>stunning low-poly 3D</strong>, right on your personal computer.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/97667e522e42d5c136405c093346e34b.poster.avif?t=1757698469\" width=480 height=360 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/97667e522e42d5c136405c093346e34b.webm?t=1757698469\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/extras/97667e522e42d5c136405c093346e34b.mp4?t=1757698469\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3784300?t=1757698469","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3784300?t=1757698469","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/090b721f09921715f7d223cd34edf49cd34bcced/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1757698469","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3784300/090b721f09921715f7d2